<section class="section" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="head">
    <p class="eyebrow">The free core</p>
    <h2 id="features-title">Open source, with a working app included.</h2>
    <p>Sign-in, companies, roles, email, files and the app shell are ready. Your apps add only their own features.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bento">
    <article class="card s7">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agents with limits</p>
      <h3>An agent that waits for you.</h3>
      <p>Tell the Projects agent what to do in plain words. It never does more than your role allows.</p>
      <div class="key run viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="run-top"><span>Agent run · Spring season</span><span><b>Role</b> · member</span></div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="key step">read<small>12 tasks</small></div>
          <div class="key step">plan<small>3 changes</small></div>
          <div class="key step wait">delete<small>needs you</small></div>
          <div class="key step now">move<small>running</small></div>
          <div class="key step">log<small>queued</small></div>
        </div>
        <div class="run-foot"><span>approvals · 1 waiting</span><span class="ok">logged · every action</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s5">
      <p class="eyebrow">Bring your own AI</p>
      <h3>Your model, your key.</h3>
      <p>Workers AI is the default, so you need no other key. Or bring your own.</p>
      <div class="tiles viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="key tile on"><i></i>Workers AI</div>
        <div class="key tile on"><i></i>Claude</div>
        <div class="key tile"><i></i>OpenAI</div>
        <div class="key tile on"><i></i>Gateway</div>
        <div class="key tile"><i></i>Vectorize</div>
        <div class="key tile"><i></i>Your key</div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s4">
      <p class="eyebrow">Many companies</p>
      <h3>One install, many teams.</h3>
      <p>Each company has its own people, projects, logo and workspaces.</p>
      <div class="rows viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="key rowk">Northwind Theater<span class="chip ok">owner</span></div>
        <div class="key rowk">Harbor Studio<span class="chip">member</span></div>
        <div class="key rowk">Cedar &amp; Co.<span class="chip">guest</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s4">
      <p class="eyebrow">No seats</p>
      <h3>Invite anyone.</h3>
      <p>No seat limits. Invite people by email.</p>
      <div class="big"><b>$0</b><span>per person</span><span class="chip ok">free core</span></div>
      <div class="bars" aria-hidden="true"><i style="height: 28%"></i><i style="height: 36%"></i><i style="height: 44%"></i><i style="height: 52%"></i><i style="height: 66%"></i><i style="height: 78%"></i><i style="height: 100%"></i></div>
      <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true"><span>team size</span><span>price stays the same</span></div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s4">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your Cloudflare account</p>
      <h3>Your data stays yours.</h3>
      <p>Deploy with one click. Nobody else holds your data.</p>
      <div class="stack viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="key">D1<span>database</span></div>
        <div class="key">R2<span>files</span></div>
        <div class="key">Workers<span>app and API</span></div>
        <div class="key">Durable Objects<span>live rooms</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s12 edge" id="workspaces">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Companies and workspaces</p>
        <h3>One install. Many companies. Many brands.</h3>
        <p>Each company has its own people, roles and plan. Inside a company, split the work into workspaces: brands, business units, locations or regions. The same team switches between them from one menu.</p>
        <p>Apps choose their scope. Workspace-aware apps, such as Projects and Docs, keep their work per workspace. Company-wide apps, such as eSign, serve the whole company. An app builder opts in with one line in the app manifest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="rows tree">
          <div class="key rowk">Acme Holdings<span class="chip ok">company</span></div>
          <div class="key rowk ws">Acme<span class="chip">brand · default</span></div>
          <div class="key rowk ws">Acme Health<span class="chip">business unit</span></div>
          <div class="key rowk ws">Acme West<span class="chip">region</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scopes">
          <span class="key scope">Projects<small>workspace</small></span>
          <span class="key scope">Docs<small>workspace</small></span>
          <span class="key scope">eSign<small>company</small></span>
          <span class="key scope">Your app<small>you choose</small></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s12 edge" id="edge">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cloudflare's edge network</p>
        <h3>Your app runs near each person.</h3>
        <p>OpenAct runs on Cloudflare Workers. Each request runs in the Cloudflare data center closest to the person who sends it. You manage no servers and pick no region for the app.</p>
        <p>Your data has one home. The D1 database and each live room stay in one place, so every person sees the same up-to-date work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="pops">
          <div class="key pop"><b>MNL</b>Manila<span>runs here</span></div>
          <div class="key pop"><b>SJC</b>San Jose<span>runs here</span></div>
          <div class="key pop"><b>LHR</b>London<span>runs here</span></div>
          <div class="key pop"><b>GRU</b>São Paulo<span>runs here</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="link"></div>
        <div class="key home"><div>D1 and live rooms<span>one home for your data</span></div><span class="chip ok">your account</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card s12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Also in the free core</p>
      <dl class="feats">
        <div class="feat"><dt>Roles and permissions</dt><dd>Owners choose what each role can do in each app.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Sign-in without passwords</dt><dd>People get a 6-digit code by email.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Kanban, Gantt and calendar</dt><dd>Drag cards, bars and dates.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Approvals</dt><dd>Deletes and people changes wait for a person.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Agent log</dt><dd>OpenAct records each action that the agent does.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Search by meaning</dt><dd>Type "venue" to find "Book the gala hall".</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Live updates</dt><dd>Every open page shows changes at once.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Secret projects</dt><dd>Only invited people see them.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Attachments</dt><dd>Files up to 25 MB on a task.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>App directory</dt><dd>Add an app with one command.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Light and dark themes</dt><dd>Or follow the system setting.</dd></div>
        <div class="feat"><dt>Known parts</dt><dd>shadcn/ui, Tailwind CSS and AG-UI.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
